---
layout: base.njk
pageType: home
title: proofstone — engineering roadmaps where every milestone is a proof
description: Engineering roadmaps where every milestone is a proof — a verifiable artifact, not a keyword. Built for working engineers.
---
{#- The page is a register: the shape of the argument is thesis → the roadmaps
    themselves, as rows → the shapes those roadmaps have → one real milestone →
    how the format works. Nothing stands between a visitor and a roadmap.
    Every number here is computed. Hardcoding them is how this project burned
    twice (27→33, 21→20), so the only literals below are words. #}
<div class="home">

<section class="hero">
  <p class="kicker">engineering roadmaps &#183; <b>{{ liveRoadmaps.length }} live</b> &#183; {{ reviewRoadmaps.length }} in review</p>
  {#- The tagline's essential clause, with its one word in the accent. Mono,
      because this heading is the site speaking about itself — the only Sans
      headings on the site are the ones inside a rendered README. #}
  <h1 class="hero__title">Every milestone is a <em>proof</em>.</h1>
  <p class="hero__sub">{{ site.seriesLine }} {{ site.thesisSub }}</p>
  <p class="hero__prompt"><b>$</b> you're done when the artifact exists — not when the reading does</p>
</section>

{#- ── The registry ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Rows, not cards: five directions read in one pass down the numbers. Live and
    in-review sit in the same list because they are the same series — what
    separates them is the chip, which is the honest difference, not a shelf. #}
<section aria-labelledby="registry-heading">
  <div class="sec-head">
    <h2 class="kicker" id="registry-heading">the registry</h2>
    <p class="sec-head__aside">{{ roadmaps.length }} roadmaps &#183; {{ roadmaps | sumBy("milestones") }} milestones</p>
  </div>
  <ol class="registry">
    {%- for r in roadmaps %}
    <li class="registry__item">
      {#- `order` is the registry's own field, printed with a leading zero: it is
          a shelf mark, not a ranking. #}
      <span class="registry__no">{% if r.order < 10 %}0{% endif %}{{ r.order }}</span>
      <span class="registry__title">
        {%- if r.status == "live" %}<a href="/{{ r.slug }}/">{{ r.title | replace(" Roadmap", "") }}</a>
        {%- else %}{{ r.title | replace(" Roadmap", "") }}{% endif %}
      </span>
      <span class="registry__meta">
        <span><span class="n">{{ r.milestones }}</span> milestones &#183; <span class="n">{{ r | roadmapStars }}</span> flagship</span>
        {%- if r.status == "live" %}<span class="chip chip--live">live</span>
        {%- else %}<span class="chip chip--review">in review</span>{% endif %}
      </span>
      {#- The card line, not the tagline: the taglines run 130–177 characters and
          are still carried by og:description and the roadmap page itself. #}
      <p class="registry__desc">{{ r.cardLine }}{% if r.status != "live" %} Private until published.{% endif %}</p>
      {%- if r.lab %}
      <p class="registry__lab"><span class="registry__lab-tag">lab</span><a href="{{ r.lab.url }}" rel="noopener"><code>{{ r.lab.name }}</code></a> — {{ r.lab.note }}.</p>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- if r.labNote %}
      <p class="registry__lab"><span class="registry__lab-tag">lab</span>{{ r.labNote }}.</p>
      {%- endif %}
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>

{#- ── The shapes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    The silhouettes are DERIVED from each roadmap's own assets/roadmap.svg — the
    same geometry the roadmap page inlines — so this section cannot advertise a
    shape a map does not have. Monochrome and static: the drawing animation is a
    separate wave. #}
<section aria-labelledby="maps-heading">
  <div class="sec-head">
    <h2 class="kicker" id="maps-heading">the maps</h2>
    <p class="sec-head__aside">each one its own shape</p>
  </div>
  <div class="maps">
    {%- for r in liveRoadmaps %}
    <div class="map-card">
      <a href="/{{ r.slug }}/">
        <div class="map-card__frame">{{ r | roadmapSilhouette | safe }}</div>
        <p class="map-card__cap">
          <span class="map-card__no">no. {% if r.order < 10 %}0{% endif %}{{ r.order }}</span>
          <span class="map-card__name">{{ r.slug }}</span>
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

{#- ── One real milestone ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Rendered from a real README by the same pipeline as the roadmap pages, so the
    home page SHOWS the format instead of describing it — and cannot show a
    format the pages do not use. The milestone is named in the registry
    (sampleMilestone), so which one appears is a registry decision and the build
    fails if it stops resolving. #}
<section aria-labelledby="sample-heading">
  <div class="sec-head">
    <h2 class="kicker" id="sample-heading">what one milestone looks like</h2>
    <p class="sec-head__aside">taken from a live map, as rendered</p>
  </div>
  <div class="prose sample__block">
    {%- for r in liveRoadmaps %}{% if r.sampleMilestone %}{{ r | milestoneSample(r.sampleMilestone) | safe }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p class="sample__note">That is the whole format.</p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="how-heading">
  <div class="sec-head">
    <h2 class="kicker" id="how-heading">how it works</h2>
  </div>
  <ol class="how">
    <li><span class="how__n">1</span><p><b>You're done when …</b> — each node states one finishing condition, in advance.</p></li>
    <li><span class="how__n">2</span><p><b>An artifact.</b> Meeting it leaves something outside your head — a merged eval, a green test suite, a fabricated board.</p></li>
    <li><span class="how__n">3</span><p><b>Proof.</b> The artifact is the evidence. Nothing here is finished by reading about it.</p></li>
  </ol>
</section>

{#- Related work, in the register's own language rather than a card: there is one
    companion, and a bordered box for it read as a sixth roadmap that had lost
    its numbers. The owner is spelled out in the link text on purpose — this
    repository lives in a personal account, not in the proofstone org. #}
<section aria-labelledby="companion-heading">
  <div class="sec-head">
    <h2 class="kicker" id="companion-heading">companion projects</h2>
    <p class="sec-head__aside">alongside the series &#183; no milestones</p>
  </div>
  {#- One line and one sentence, the same shape a roadmap gets in the register
      above. The long version of this note lived here when the block was a card;
      the repository says it better than a paragraph on someone else's site can,
      and the AI Safety map already states the relation from the inside. #}
  <div class="companion">
    <span class="companion__tag">index</span>
    <div>
      <h3 class="companion__name"><a href="https://github.com/TheSeydiCharyyev/build-your-own-agent" rel="noopener">TheSeydiCharyyev/build-your-own-agent</a></h3>
      <p class="companion__note">
        An index, not a map: for each of the ten components of the agent stack it points at the best
        from-scratch tutorial that exists — and ships a runnable one of its own for the three where
        none did.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="home__note">
    The roadmap repositories are the source of truth — this site is the render layer.
    Contribute by opening a pull request on a roadmap's repo; the site rebuilds itself.
  </p>
</section>

</div>
